SUMMARY:ABO 80's Double Feature for Disability Awareness: Celebrating 100 Years of Durham Athletic Park (DAP)
DESCRIPTION:PLAY BALL\, Durham! Alternative Baseball celebrates the 100th Year Anniversary of the Durham Athletic Park from Bull Durham. On November 7th\, the national ABO is hosting a 9-inning event at the DAP starring athletes with disabilities from across the East Coast who will play alongside/against local community leaders and former pros to promote awareness for disability integration/opportunity! Former Bulls owner\, the trailblazer of the Durham Bulls\, Miles Wolff\, will throw out the ceremonial first pitch. Wool E. Bull will also be joining the day’s events. First pitch time is at 12:05 ET start time. More information about how to RSVP to spectate or volunteer can be found at www.alternativebaseball.org or by calling (770)313-1762. Free admission with donations encouraged.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/abo-80s-double-feature-for-disability-awareness-celebrating-100-years-of-durham-athletic-park-dap/
LOCATION:Historic Durham Athletic Park\, 500 W. Corporation St.\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement,Sports
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/GOES-TO-2.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Alternative Baseball (ABO)":MAILTO:taylor@alternativebaseball.org
GEO:36.00285;-78.902568
